    <section class="mbt__accordion" aria-label="Brightness Test FAQs">
      <h2 class="mbt__sectionTitle">Brightness Test FAQs</h2>

      <details>
        <summary>What is the Monroe Brightness Test?</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>It is a quick check that helps you spot uneven digit brightness across a calculator display by comparing the far left and far right digits.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What does fading from left to right mean?</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>It typically indicates display wear from years of extended use where digits stay illuminated for long periods.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I fix a dim or uneven display?</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>In most cases, display fading is not cost-effective to repair. Replacement is usually the most reliable option for clear readability.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What other signs tell me it's time to replace my calculator?</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Common indicators include missing digits on the display, blank spaces on the printed audit trail, sticky or unresponsive keys, or worn key symbols.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="mbt__accordion" aria-label="Additional signs your calculator should be replaced">
      <h2 class="mbt__sectionTitle">Additional Signs Your Calculator Should Be Replaced</h2>

      <details>
        <summary>Printing and Display Issues</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>If a digit or function entry does not appear on the display, the key may not be making proper contact.</li>
          <li>If the printed audit trail shows a blank space where a digit should be, the printer may be dropping digits and starting to fail.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Keyboard Issues</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>
            If keys feel flimsy or less responsive, consider upgrading to the
            <a href="/products/monroe-ultimatex-12-digit-programmable-heavy-duty-accounting-printing-calculator-with-edit-reprint-capabilities" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UltimateX</a>.
            It uses
            <a href="/blogs/news/the-monroe-difference-a-lifelong-investment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">independent key switch technology (IKT)</a>
            for a softer, more responsive touch.
          </li>
          <li>If key symbols are worn off, it is often a sign the unit has seen heavy use. Monroe heavy duty calculators use long lasting key tops designed for longevity.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </section>

